fbc_preview.description:
PV format, timezone-aware timestamps, 15-minute intervals and full next-72-hour coverage passed. Any selected load input also passed its coverage and interval checks.

PV power type: {pv_type}
PV intervals: {count}
Start: {start}
End: {end}
Peak PV power: {peak} W
PV energy over the displayed period: {energy} kWh
PV source age (information only): {age} minutes
Building load: {load}

Timestamps use UTC. FBC plans through local midnight. No load selection keeps the original PV-only calculation; selecting load feeds predicted PV surplus into the same calculation engine.

import_preview.description:
The forecast format, 15-minute continuity, complete next 72 hours passed.

Validated intervals: {count}
Start: {start}
End: {end}
Peak power: {peak} W
Energy over this period: {energy} kWh
Source age (information only): {age} minutes

Timestamps use UTC. Submit to register this shared input. The source is checked again before saving and whenever it changes, and at least once a minute. Multiple modules can use this input.

import_value_preview.description:
Format, finite numeric values, 15-minute continuity and full next-72-hour coverage passed.

Intervals: {count}
Start: {start}
End: {end}
Minimum: {minimum} {unit}
Maximum: {maximum} {unit}
Source age (information only): {age} minutes

Timestamps use UTC. Submit to register. The source is checked again before saving, on source changes and at least once a minute.

thermal_cost_inputs.description:
Select reusable registrations from BEMS forecast importer. PV must be AC power on the same basis as the electrical loads. Optional building load is subtracted first; exclude the thermal tasks being costed. Grid electricity uses the import price; self-consumed PV uses the lost export revenue. Each setup evaluates PV independently; no shared PV reservations or battery effects are simulated.

If export is limited, PV surplus above that limit uses the curtailed-PV price (usually zero). With this option off, the limit and curtailed-PV price are ignored. A limit of zero explicitly means no export.

{reason}

thermal_cost_preview.description:
Current cost: {current} EUR/timestep
Range: {minimum} to {maximum} EUR/timestep
Current COP: {cop}
COP fallback intervals: {fallback}
Fallback reason: {reason}
Intervals: {count}
UTC coverage: {start} to {end}

Each value is the cost of one complete 15-minute activation, including any additional electrical power. The current state equals the first forecast value. This is an independent cost estimate, not a heating schedule. Submit to save; inputs are checked again.

